WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back!
-Hello!

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:03.636
-I always -- I want to start by
saying thank you, of course,

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, of course, you have
a show tonight.

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:08.608
You're making time for us.
I really appreciate that.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.142 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's all right.

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ten news stories will break
between this moment.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So in a way,
I'm doing you a favor

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
because if you were at work
right now,

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
you would be writing something
that would already be old

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.418 line:92%
by the time you're on at 9:00.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:18.852 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:19.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I'm just giving you
an hour off.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know there --
I'm a disorganized person.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.189 line:92%
And I have bad time management.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I've always
had this problem

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.626
ever since I started doing work
like this,

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:29.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I produce stuff that
doesn't make it on to the show

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.964 size:81% position:41%
for whatever reason --
other stuff goes long

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:33.666
or I can't end an interview on
time -- I have no discipline.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.969
So there's always been some
stuff I have to kick out.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:40.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
But now every single day,
the entire show I throw away

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.643
two hours before air time and
have to invent a whole new one.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like I should just
come in at 8:00

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
before the 9:00 show
and be like, "Hit me now!

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:51.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hit me now! I'm just going to
ad-lib the whole thing."

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
I threw away a whole show
every day.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.154 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It is nuts.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.155 line:92%
This is an unprecedented time.

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:58.324
And it has affected not only
our show, not only your show,

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:02.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it actually affected
your signoff the other night.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:02.896 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, God.

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.631 line:92%
Yeah, you know, there are --

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:08.168
Like, throughout the history of
people doing news on television,

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:10.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
there has been all these,
like, really noble signoffs --

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:13.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
"courage," you know,
"good night and good luck."

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-People do, like, you know?

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:17.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's been all these
very serious ones.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
And people don't necessarily
try them anymore.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:22.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have inadvertently
developed one

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:24.984 size:75% position:38%
that I started doing
without trying to.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:29.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It started when I was talking
about Steve Bannon,

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:32.358
the White House strategist guy.
You know, the grim reaper guy?

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It already feels like
a million years ago, yeah.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:35.328 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I know.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.764 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He was in Congress.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:40.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he wasn't answering
their questions

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
because his lawyer
was advising him not to.

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
And his lawyer
was advising him not to

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he was on the phone
with the White House.

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:47.440 line:92%
And the White House was saying,

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We don't want Steve
answering those questions."

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.879
Turns out Steve Bannon's lawyer
is also the lawyer

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the guy at the White House
he was talking to.

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:57.117
-So, here's your new signoff,
which I think -- I don't know.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's as good as
all of them.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-Let's take a look.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:03.156
-Having somebody on those two
different sides of the story

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:06.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
both represented
by the same attorney?

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:10.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's weird.
That does it for us tonight.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:10.930 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.766
-"That's weird. Good night."
-"That's weird. Good night!"

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah. Sleep well.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:19.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm sure you'll talk about
this, this evening.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:20.406 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The memo.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
We talked a little bit
about the memo.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think the release of
this memo,

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
which seems inevitable
at this point,

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:27.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you think it will escalate
the investigation

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:31.217
into Trump and Russia ties,
if that's even possible?

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:34.387
Or do you think the takeaway,
when we look back on this memo,

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.856
will be this was a degrading of
our institutions

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
that someone in Congress
would basically

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:41.761
go after the Justice Department
and the FBI like this?

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.530 line:92%
-Well, the memo isn't part of --

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.466 size:84% position:42%
It isn't like something
that's been revealed

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.367 size:84% position:42% line:92%
from the investigation.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
The memo is part of
the Trump White House

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the Trump supporters
in Congress

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.940
trying to make the investigation
go away.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.043
So this is part of their defense
against the investigation.

00:02:57.043 --> 00:03:00.480
And there was a guy who was
a part of the Trump campaign,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.581 line:92%
he was a foreign adviser --

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
foreign policy adviser
to the campaign.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:07.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he had been caught up
in a Russian spy ring

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.054 line:92%
in New York City in 2013.

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:09.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, like, FBI
counterintelligence

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:12.125
had been involved in, like,
breaking up the spy ring.

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:14.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
And people went to prison.
And it was for real.

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then he turns up
on the Trump campaign,

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.398 size:75% position:38%
and in the middle of
the Trump campaign,

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:21.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
he goes to Russia and gives
an anti-U.S./pro-Putin speech.

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:24.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, like, the
counterintelligence folks

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.004 line:92%
are interested in this guy

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they're supposed to
monitor people

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
who might be foreign agents
in the United States.

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:31.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they got warrants
to surveil him

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:32.779 line:92%
starting during the campaign.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:34.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it got renewed
a bunch of times,

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:35.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
including into
the Trump campaign.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:39.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
This whole memo thing is about
trying to make it a scandal

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:42.889
that it was renewed the most
recent time it was renewed.

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:43.323 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:46.426
-"And that means there should be
no investigation."

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:47.126 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It's like, "No, dude."

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.796
You had the guy with the Russian
spies working on --

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:52.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then going to Moscow
and being like,

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:53.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I love Putin.
I hate America."

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:56.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, of course, the FBI is
gonna look into him.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:57.403 line:92%
So they're gonna try to say

00:03:57.403 --> 00:04:00.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
that means there shouldn't be
a Russia investigation.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:03.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's been
a very big distraction,

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:04.010 line:92%
which I think is effective.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:08.281
But I don't think it will --
I don't think it will change

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
anything on Robert Mueller's
to-do list.

